        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "80961bf4ea8841afb7639"
    },
    {
      "text": "####Inner join\n>Spark Inner join is the default join and it’s mostly used, It is used to join two DataFrames/Datasets on key columns, and where keys don’t match the rows get dropped from both datasets (emp & dept).",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "1456bea025314ab8bd053"
    },
    {
      "text": "#### 2. Handling Duplicate Column Names\n>dealing with duplicate column names in your\nresults DataFrame. In a DataFrame, each column has a unique ID within Spark’s SQL Engine,\nCatalyst. This unique ID is purely internal and not something that you can directly reference.\nThis makes it quite difficult to refer to a specific column when you have a DataFrame with\nduplicate column names.\nThis can occur in two distinct situations:\n\n1. The join expression that you specify does not remove one key from one of the input\nDataFrames and the keys have the same column name\n2. Two columns on which you are not performing the join have the same name\nLet’s create a problem dataset that we can use to illustrate these problems",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "4b01767297d047dca9fde"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "09d387ea92994328a6563"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nperson.join(gradProgramDupe, joinExpr).drop(person.col(\"graduate_program\")).select(\"graduate_program\").show()\n\nval joinExpr = person.col(\"graduate_program\") === graduateProgram.col(\"id\")\nperson.join(graduateProgram, joinExpr).drop(graduateProgram.col(\"id\")).show()",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "59787fac09bb45cfbd90b"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n  val emp = Seq((1,\"Smith\",1,\"10\",3000),\n    (2,\"Rose\",1,\"20\",4000),\n    (3,\"Williams\",1,\"10\",1000),\n    (4,\"Jones\",2,\"10\",2000),\n    (5,\"Brown\",2,\"40\",-1),\n    (6,\"Brown\",2,\"50\",-1)\n  )\n  val empColumns = Seq(\"emp_id\",\"name\",\"superior_emp_id\",\"emp_dept_id\",\"salary\")\n  import spark.implicits._\n  val empDF = emp.toDF(empColumns:_*)\n  empDF.show(false)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "7baa6a1913f94b3cb907b"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n \n //“emp_dept_id” 5o doesn’t have a record on “dept” dataset hence, this record contains null on “dept” columns (dept_name & dept_id). and “dept_id” 30 from “dept” dataset dropped from the results\n empDF.join(deptDF,empDF(\"emp_dept_id\") ===  deptDF(\"dept_id\"),\"left\")\n    .show(false)",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
